Package: IWEE
Type: Package
Title: Inverse-Weighted Estimating Equations for Zero-Inflated Microbiome Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    c(
    person(given = "Tingchang",
           family = "Wang",
           role = "aut",
           email = "twang5@ufl.edu"),
    person(given = "Zhigang",
           family = "Li",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "zhigang.li@ufl.edu")
    )
Description: Implements an inverse-weighted estimating equation (IWEE)
    approach for identifying microbial taxa associated with covariates of
    interest in zero-inflated, compositional microbiome data. Zeros are
    modeled as a mixture of biological zeros and zeros induced by the
    sampling mechanism. The package selects the zero-mechanism parameter by
    cross-validation, screens reference taxa with a LASSO, estimates
    coefficients with weighted least squares (optionally via QR
    decomposition), and obtains jackknife bias-corrected estimates, variances,
    p-values and false discovery rate adjusted significance calls. Group-wise
    computations are run in parallel.
